  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nVery broad area of upper ridging remains in place Mid Atlantic\nStates through the Southern Plains with an upper low over the\nPacific Northwest. Meanwhile, what is left of Edouard is still\nspinning over southeast TX. \n\nWe had a few showers early this morning west of I-135 along a\nmid level baroclinic zone. Not expecting this same scenario Fri\nmorning, as the better mid level moisture transport shifts\nslightly west. Unfortunately upper ridging is expected to \namplify across the Plains as we head into the weekend which will\nkeep the unseasonably hot temperatures in place. \n\nThere is decent model agreement in an upper impulse lifting out\nof the Pacific Northwest and into the Northern Rockies by Tue \nmorning. As this wave continues to slide east, it will allow a \ncold front to push through the Northern and Central Plains, but \nunfortunately doesn't look to make it into central KS. With \ncompressional heating effects, it looks like Tue may be one of \nthe hotter days through this forecast package. Persistent upper\nridge will remain in place for the mid to end of next week, \nkeeping daily highs around 100, which is around 10-13 degrees \nabove normal highs for this time of year.",
